{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The Fiedler vector of a connected graph: a unit eigenvector of λ₂, the algebraic"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"connectivity, of the Laplacian (or of the normalized Laplacian), with one entry per vertex."}],"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"title":"Conforms To","kind":"relationships","type":"conformsTo"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/FiedlerVector"},"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory"]]},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/FiedlerVector\/algebraicConnectivity","doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/FiedlerVector\/values"],"title":"Instance Properties","anchor":"Instance-Properties","generated":true},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/FiedlerVector\/value(of:)","doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/FiedlerVector\/value(ofIndex:)"],"title":"Instance Methods","anchor":"Instance-Methods","generated":true}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/spectralgraphtheory\/fiedlervector"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"metadata":{"externalID":"s:19SpectralGraphTheory13FiedlerVectorV","role":"symbol","symbolKind":"struct","roleHeading":"Structure","title":"FiedlerVector","modules":[{"name":"SpectralGraphTheory"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"FiedlerVector"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"FiedlerVector.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/SpectralGraphTheory\/FiedlerVector.swift#L15"},"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"FiedlerVector"}]},"primaryContentSections